    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are many ways to prevent food waste. For example, we could buy only what we need or use "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " products first. But the French city of Colmar has a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "genius",
            "ref": "v-genius"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " idea. In 2015, it started "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " free chickens to its residents."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The project had been in the works for some time. "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Then-mayor",
            "zh": "时任市长"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Gilbert Meyer had run for office again the year before with the slogan “one family, one hen”. Once in office, he put it into practice by working with two chicken farms. He told residents that "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a chicken would pay off quickly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "At first, more than 200 homes from four of the city’s districts signed up. Each was given two chickens after "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to do a good job. The project turned out to be a big success and is still going "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “Over the years, other districts have joined in,” says Eric Straumann, the current mayor of Colmar. “Since 2022, all 20 of our districts have taken part.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But don’t think of getting the chickens just for the free eggs. Officials from the waste department come and "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the chickens’ "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "condition",
            "ref": "v-condition"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They also make sure that each home has enough space for the animals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "To date, they have given more than five thousand chickens to homes. The animals are fed on kitchen scraps, and food waste has been greatly "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “A chicken lives up to four years on average and eats 150g of bio-waste per day,” says Straumann. “This means that we have "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " about 273.35 tonnes of waste in the last ten years.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There’s a deeper "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for the effort. Food waste decays quickly and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "releases",
            "ref": "v-release"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " more methane into the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "atmosphere",
            "ref": "v-atmosphere"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " than any other type of waste. The gas has a greater long-term global warming effect than CO₂. Today, around a third of the world’s food is "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or wasted every year. That "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "accounts for",
            "zh": "占"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " 8 to 10 per cent of global greenhouse gas emissions. It’s worth the effort to prevent as much food as possible from going to waste."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
